    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6811" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακροτέω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lift up and strike together,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὼ χεῖρ᾽ ἀνεκρότησ᾽ ὑφ᾽ ἡδονῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					739
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακροτήσας τὰς χεῖρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					2.226
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς χερσὶν ὑφ᾽ ἡδονῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Mar.</u>
					44
				</span></i>
			: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ δ᾽ ἀνεκρότησαν</span>”
				<i>applauded vehemently,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					651
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>V.</u>
				1314
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				12.4.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				1.39
			</span></i>: aor.
			part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακορτήσασα</span> cj. in Hexam. ap.
				<i><span class="en">
				Diogenian.
				3.67
			</span></i>.</div>
